---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Anim from "../../components/Anim.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="@open-rgs/pay-cluster  - Connected groups"
  description="Pay-cluster: A wild belongs to every cluster it touches."
>
  <main>
    <p class="dim"><a href="/extension">&larr; extensions</a></p>
    <h1>@open-rgs/pay-cluster</h1>

    <p class="lede">A wild belongs to every cluster it touches.</p>

    <Anim kind="pay-cluster" caption="Orthogonal only - diagonals do not connect. The outlined wild is counted in both the teal group and the amber one." />

    <p>Which is the whole difficulty. The flood fill runs per symbol and consumes only real matches - consume the wild for the first cluster and the second silently shrinks by one, with nothing on the board looking wrong. A cluster is never seeded from a wild either.</p>

    <h2 data-section="&sect;">Reach for</h2>
    <pre><code>{`import { ... } from "@open-rgs/pay-cluster";`}</code></pre>
    <p class="dim">clustersOf  &middot;  evalClusters  &middot;  evalAllClusters  &middot;  largestCluster</p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
